Z||000000||Flamberge||10-17-2001||12:10 AM||||I don't own a garage, and park on the street. My 88GT is the third Fiero I have had, the first being in Alaska. (One storm covered it in over three feet of snow.) This new one was a one owner garage-kept car. Because of that, it is in very good condition.<P>So...does anyone have any ideas for me on how to protect (as much as possible) this new Fiero against the elements this winter? I live in Colorado, so we do good cold and snow in moderation. I am thinking a car cover, but that wouldn't be economical from a day-to-day stand point, since it is my daily driver.<P>Anything previous experience would be great. (Driving in the ice and snow is no problem, as I never once got stuck/lost control/spun out/etc. in three winters in Anchorage.)<P>*wish I had a garage*<BR>- Flamberge ||||reg||5
